        "id": 24611,
        "name": "Ronway",
        "username": "Ronway",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/ronway/{size}/1856_2.png",
        "created_at": "2011-12-15T15:16:21.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>It depends on the exact wording of the card. If it says “strike the hero with the highest HP x damage then the second highest with y damage” then the highest would be chosen to taken between the two, lets say A takes the damage. So then the second attack would follow after the first damage and who ever is the second at that point would take the damage. Now if the wording was “The highest and second highest HP target takes x damage” then I would take it as the two tied for the highest.</p>\n<p>Edit: Not an official ruling, just the way I always saw it as.</p>",
        "post_number": 2,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:58:35.320Z",
