        "id": 24612,
        "name": "awp832",
        "username": "awp832",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/a/a9a28c/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2011-12-15T15:27:30.000Z",
        "cooked": "<ol>\n<li>\n<p>A&amp;B are the highest and the second highest, as they are tied.      Recall though, if you aren’t already, that the Villan character card counts as a Target for the purposes of most things, including the T-Rex.    The situation where this question would need to be resolved seems like it would be extremely unlikely to occur,  although it is possible.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>That makes no sense whatesoever.    You mean…  if 2 heroes are tied for HP and are the only possible targets, can you assign the attack to one of them and redirect it to the other?  I’d say not.    If you choose a hero as having the highest HP for purposes of an attack, then he has the highest HP for purposes of that attack.</p>\n</li>\n</ol>",
        "post_number": 3,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:58:35.389Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
