        "id": 24615,
        "name": "TheJayMann",
        "username": "TheJayMann",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/thejaymann/{size}/2261_2.png",
        "created_at": "2011-12-16T11:48:25.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>If only two “targetable” targets are tied, I see no reason that choosing one as the “highest” at one point in any way requires you to continue designating it as the highest during a later targeting.  In other words, a single target in this situation can be the highest according to one card while being the lowest according to another, even if the latter is acting in response to actions in the former.</p>",
        "post_number": 6,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:58:35.641Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
